# Shell scripts must keep LF everywhere: a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf
# would otherwise give them CRLF, and bash (Git Bash included) then fails on
# the stray \r. Batch files are the reverse - cmd.exe misreads some LF-only
# files, so they are checked out with CRLF on every OS.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
